SYLVIA_GM_ENGINE_TURN_CONTROL (application-owned, not player speech):
{"required_before_narration":[{"description":"Advance the turn.","operation":"advance_turn","provider_tool_name":"tool_a_advance"},{"description":"End — now ünïcode.","operation":"end_encounter","provider_tool_name":"tool_b_end"}]}
Read the fresh player instruction before advancing combat. Before any player-facing narration, call the exact listed provider tool using authoritative state. If the established scene instead requires ending the encounter, call the currently exposed end-encounter operation. Do not print or simulate either operation.

SYLVIA_GM_CAMPAIGN_PREPARATION (application-owned control, not player speech):
{"queue": [{"actor": "pc-1", "event": "choose_kit"}], "ünï": "ok"}
Resolve the first actor's queued events in order through the declared normal intent. Ask the player for unresolved required choices in OOC; never invent their selections. Obtain the ordinary confirmation for each event. Respect a declined proposal; ask what should change instead of automatically repeating it. Keep original library cards unchanged. Until the queue is complete, do not start the story, advance acts, grant rewards or perform ordinary play mechanics. An OOC question with an unchanged Campaign File is allowed. Reassess fresh State after each committed event; do not repeat completed steps.

